1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,860
In Vanuatu, a village
worships a British prince.

2
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:07,224
It is Yaohnanen, high
on the island of Tanna.

3
00:00:07,744 --> 00:00:10,641
The prince is Philip, husband
of Queen Elizabeth the Second.

4
00:00:11,161 --> 00:00:15,003
The belief took off after
the royal couple visited in 1974,

5
00:00:15,023 --> 00:00:16,770
aboard the yacht Britannia.

6
00:00:17,290 --> 00:00:19,562
Prince Philip never set foot on Tanna.

7
00:00:20,082 --> 00:00:25,095
Some say it grew from an older story
of a pale man who rose from a volcano.

8
00:00:25,615 --> 00:00:30,178
In a thatched hut, villagers keep his
portrait, and wait for him to return.

9
00:00:30,698 --> 00:00:34,454
So why would a village wait
for a prince who never came?

